     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">\r\nHi Shu,\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Apologies for my late reply. You can read in the table in R and get the log ratio of the raw_cov and norm_cov, followed by taking the log transformation. Or if you prefer, you can load your output table into Excel and add a column in Excel which\r\n seems to be easier.</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Cheers,</div>\r\n<div>Yuchao</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n<div>\r\n<blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n<div>On Jul 5, 2016, at 3:31 PM, Tao, Shu &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">sh...@coh.org</a>&gt; wrote:</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\nHi Yuchao,<u></u><u></u></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<u></u> <u></u></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<u></u> <u></u></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\nThe following are column names from CODEX output. In copy_no, 1 or 0 indicates deletion and any value large than 3 indicates duplication.<u></u><u></u></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<u></u> <u></u></div>\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" width=\"970\" style=\"width:727.35pt;border-collapse:collapse\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n<td width=\"101\" nowrap valign=\"bottom\" style=\"width:76.05pt;padding:0in 5.4pt;height:15pt\">\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\